  "biostatistical_findings": {
    "finding_1_sixty_events_uncertainty": "60 matured events DOES NOT automatically guarantee 80% power for delta = 0.05. Under the realistic panel discordant assumption p_disc = 0.10, N=60 yields only 33.72% statistical power. To achieve 80% power at delta = 0.05 with p_disc = 0.10, N_distress >= 248 failure events are required.",
    "finding_2_when_sixty_events_is_adequate": "N = 60 provides adequate power (~79% to 80%) in exactly two distinct scenarios: 1) Practical Tier: If the business adopts margin delta = 0.10 under p_disc = 0.10 (power = 78.95%). 2) Ultra-High Concordance: If discordant rate between models is very low (p_disc <= 0.0242), power reaches 80.09% at delta = 0.05.",
    "finding_3_current_cohort_n8_inadequacy": "At the current matured sample N=8, statistical power is only 11.55% for delta = 0.05 and 22.65% for delta = 0.10. Testing for non-inferiority with N=8 is completely indefensible from a biostatistical standpoint."
  }
